<title>USA: U.S. Stockpile gets the lead (1,330 tonnes) out.</title>
<headline>U.S. Stockpile gets the lead (1,330 tonnes) out.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Defense National Stockpile Center said it sold 1,330 tonnes of lead for $861,178 at prices ranging from 29.0 to 29.8 cents a lb.</p>
<p>Specialty Metals &amp; Minerals bought 500 tonnes, Canfield Technologies 60 tonnes, and  East Penn Manufacturing 770 tonnes.</p>
<p>The next bids for lead will be accepted Aug 7.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212-859-1646))</p>
</text>
